WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.844 --> 00:00:03.416
- She's healthier than me.

00:00:03.416 --> 00:00:05.833
(rock music)

00:00:07.104 --> 00:00:08.525
- Ever since I can remember,

00:00:08.525 --> 00:00:10.622
I have made a conscious effort in my life

00:00:10.622 --> 00:00:13.509
to have a incredibly
clean and healthy diet.

00:00:13.509 --> 00:00:14.342
I am vegan

00:00:14.342 --> 00:00:16.426
and I tend not to eat too much gluten.

00:00:16.426 --> 00:00:18.928
- Eating food is equal to happiness,

00:00:18.928 --> 00:00:21.736
so I really need to focus
on eating what I like.

00:00:21.736 --> 00:00:23.140
A lot of junk food, usually.

00:00:23.140 --> 00:00:25.817
- My mom was really into health,

00:00:25.817 --> 00:00:27.370
and so it's something I grew up with.

00:00:27.370 --> 00:00:29.231
- I'm sure that when I
start eating healthy,

00:00:29.231 --> 00:00:30.800
it'll probably, you know,

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:32.490
do something magical?

00:00:32.490 --> 00:00:33.323
I mean if it doesn't,

00:00:33.323 --> 00:00:34.694
I'm never gonna healthy, so.

00:00:34.694 --> 00:00:36.790
I think for me it's
gonna be hard mentally.

00:00:36.790 --> 00:00:38.780
But physically it's
gonna be harder for you.

00:00:38.780 --> 00:00:40.707
- [Cameraman] Dun dun dun.

00:00:40.707 --> 00:00:43.194
- [YB] So literally all my
favorite foods in there.

00:00:43.194 --> 00:00:44.937
- Okay, pizza.

00:00:44.937 --> 00:00:45.949
Oh you put in parentheses,

00:00:45.949 --> 00:00:47.549
"I can usually eat the whole pizza."

00:00:47.549 --> 00:00:49.532
"No vegetables on it, hehehehe."

00:00:49.532 --> 00:00:50.523
(laughs)

00:00:50.523 --> 00:00:52.226
So I guess I'm eating a whole pizza.

00:00:52.226 --> 00:00:53.162
Let's go.

00:00:53.162 --> 00:00:56.135
- So breakfast smoothie, I like smoothies.

00:00:56.135 --> 00:00:59.008
Blueberries, kale, banana,

00:00:59.008 --> 00:01:00.518
wheatgrass powder.

00:01:00.518 --> 00:01:01.614
What's wheatgrass?

00:01:01.614 --> 00:01:03.317
- Wheatgrass is um,

00:01:03.317 --> 00:01:04.150
it's a grass.

00:01:04.150 --> 00:01:05.094
- So I'm eating grass.

00:01:05.094 --> 00:01:05.927
- Yeah.

00:01:05.927 --> 00:01:07.058
- I think one out of 10,

00:01:07.058 --> 00:01:08.809
I'll do maybe like eight.

00:01:08.809 --> 00:01:10.030
- I think I'm gonna do terrible.

00:01:10.030 --> 00:01:10.863
(laughs)

00:01:10.863 --> 00:01:13.274
(curious music)

00:01:13.274 --> 00:01:15.290
- So Saturday morning

00:01:15.290 --> 00:01:17.798
I went to get the smoothie
for my breakfast smoothie.

00:01:17.798 --> 00:01:19.078
And then I got a wheatgrass shot

00:01:19.078 --> 00:01:20.320
because they had it.

00:01:20.320 --> 00:01:21.465
- She's gonna have a wheatgrass shot

00:01:21.465 --> 00:01:22.760
and then you'll be like,

00:01:22.760 --> 00:01:24.966
"I can take on the world."

00:01:24.966 --> 00:01:25.936
- Ugh.

00:01:25.936 --> 00:01:27.989
It's like, not good at all.

00:01:27.989 --> 00:01:29.143
It's like warm grass.

00:01:29.143 --> 00:01:32.221
- I did the whole Saturday
morning cartoon thing

00:01:32.221 --> 00:01:34.268
in bed with my Reese's Puffs.

00:01:34.268 --> 00:01:36.850
Just really, really sugary.

00:01:36.850 --> 00:01:39.154
I don't know if I can
eat a whole bowl of this.

00:01:39.154 --> 00:01:40.175
But it's kind of good.

00:01:40.175 --> 00:01:41.576
- So it's 11:50

00:01:41.576 --> 00:01:44.916
and I finished the smoothie
while I was driving,

00:01:44.916 --> 00:01:46.595
and I am so hungry.

00:01:46.595 --> 00:01:48.663
I'm used to very carb heavy breakfast.

00:01:48.663 --> 00:01:49.770
So I was getting kinda hangry.

00:01:49.770 --> 00:01:51.950
- So I went to yoga Saturday afternoon.

00:01:51.950 --> 00:01:54.307
I was really tired during class.

00:01:54.307 --> 00:01:56.163
It's as if the sugar from the cereal

00:01:56.163 --> 00:01:57.800
just rushed to my brain.

00:01:57.800 --> 00:02:00.304
And all I wanna do is go
get a giant Green Juice

00:02:00.304 --> 00:02:02.738
to (bleep) cleanse the
sugar out of my system.

00:02:02.738 --> 00:02:05.116
- Sky is drinking something healthy.

00:02:05.116 --> 00:02:06.920
Whatcha drinkin'?

00:02:06.920 --> 00:02:09.677
(sad trombone sound)

00:02:09.677 --> 00:02:10.899
- I cheated, okay?

00:02:10.899 --> 00:02:13.598
But after dinner I made up for it.

00:02:13.598 --> 00:02:16.058
I ate a whole bunch of Doritos.

00:02:16.058 --> 00:02:17.325
I'm gonna eat so many of these.

00:02:17.325 --> 00:02:18.659
These are (bleep) amazing.

00:02:18.659 --> 00:02:19.492
Wow.

00:02:19.492 --> 00:02:20.779
- Smoothie time.

00:02:20.779 --> 00:02:21.905
Oh, it's good.

00:02:21.905 --> 00:02:23.550
Oh, I thought it was gonna
taste like really bad,

00:02:23.550 --> 00:02:24.468
but it's really good.

00:02:24.468 --> 00:02:26.061
I even went hiking with my dog,

00:02:26.061 --> 00:02:27.129
and I was like feeling good.

00:02:27.129 --> 00:02:29.811
I was like, "Yeah, I feel
healthy and I have energy!"

00:02:29.811 --> 00:02:32.914
The only sucky part was
like after I came back home,

00:02:32.914 --> 00:02:34.324
I was super hungry and, you know,

00:02:34.324 --> 00:02:35.182
and tired.

00:02:35.182 --> 00:02:36.332
But I had to cook again.

00:02:36.332 --> 00:02:37.478
- I really failed.

00:02:37.478 --> 00:02:38.311
I failed hard.

00:02:38.311 --> 00:02:39.401
I'm just gonna admit it.

00:02:39.401 --> 00:02:40.463
I should've been better.

00:02:40.463 --> 00:02:42.978
I should've stuck to the experiment more.

00:02:42.978 --> 00:02:44.722
But I felt the effects.

00:02:44.722 --> 00:02:46.056
And,

00:02:46.056 --> 00:02:47.543
Sunday night dinner,

00:02:47.543 --> 00:02:50.037
I went through the Burger King drive-thru.

00:02:50.037 --> 00:02:51.939
- You are the last person I would imagine

00:02:51.939 --> 00:02:53.999
to even accept this challenge

00:02:53.999 --> 00:02:56.627
because of how often we discuss health

00:02:56.627 --> 00:02:57.941
and how often I see you doing, like,

00:02:57.941 --> 00:02:59.059
pushups in our backyard.

00:02:59.059 --> 00:02:59.892
(laughs)

00:02:59.892 --> 00:03:04.151
- Hi, can I have a small fries and a Coke?

00:03:04.151 --> 00:03:06.774
Like I feel, if anyone saw me doing this,

00:03:06.774 --> 00:03:09.732
it would just ruin my image.

00:03:09.732 --> 00:03:10.565
French fries and ketchup,

00:03:10.565 --> 00:03:12.786
I can dig that.

00:03:12.786 --> 00:03:14.051
But I don't know, like,

00:03:14.051 --> 00:03:17.807
I don't have a burning desire
to eat the rest of this.

00:03:17.807 --> 00:03:18.811
I'm not craving this.

00:03:18.811 --> 00:03:21.264
I'm craving a Green Juice.

00:03:21.264 --> 00:03:22.667
- So,

00:03:22.667 --> 00:03:26.919
we eat the kelp noodles with pesto, salad,

00:03:26.919 --> 00:03:28.500
some kale.

00:03:28.500 --> 00:03:29.513
I want other stuff.

00:03:29.513 --> 00:03:30.744
I want, like, chicken wings.

00:03:30.744 --> 00:03:33.128
And I want burgers, pizza,

00:03:33.128 --> 00:03:34.538
other stuff to go with it.

00:03:34.538 --> 00:03:37.176
I would prefer it with
just like normal noodles.

00:03:37.176 --> 00:03:38.888
I think that would be really, really good.

00:03:38.888 --> 00:03:41.424
But this is a healthy alternative.

00:03:41.424 --> 00:03:44.558
(upbeat music)

00:03:44.558 --> 00:03:46.698
I'm really glad I did this challenge.

00:03:46.698 --> 00:03:48.311
It was a really,

00:03:48.311 --> 00:03:49.304
like I learned a lot.

00:03:49.304 --> 00:03:51.646
I learned how to cook a little bit.

00:03:51.646 --> 00:03:53.660
And I learned about a
lot of other ingredients

00:03:53.660 --> 00:03:54.726
that I didn't know about.

00:03:54.726 --> 00:03:56.799
- Like, I've realized
throughout this experience

00:03:56.799 --> 00:03:59.745
that the food that I eat

00:03:59.745 --> 00:04:01.476
is so much a part of my identity.

00:04:01.476 --> 00:04:02.798
And not having it,

00:04:02.798 --> 00:04:05.048
I feel like I'm not myself.

00:04:10.383 --> 00:04:13.012
Sweet Chili Doritos are the bomb.

00:04:13.012 --> 00:04:16.095
That's all I'm gonna say about that.

